---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const UPDATED = '20 August 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Disclaimer — TextWonder"
  description="Where TextWonder's calculators and converters should and shouldn't be relied on: financial, health, academic and legal-document tools are informational aids, not professional advice."
  canonical="/disclaimer/"
>
  <Header />

  <main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-white mb-2" style="font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;">Disclaimer</h1>
    <p class="text-slate-500 text-sm mb-8">Last updated: {UPDATED}</p>

    <div class="space-y-8 text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-2xl mb-3">General</h2>
        <p>
          Everything on TextWonder — the tools, the articles, the worked examples — is provided
          for general information and convenience. It is written carefully and tested, but it is
          not professional advice, and it does not know anything about your particular situation.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The sections below are not boilerplate. They cover the specific categories on this site
          where acting on a number without checking it could actually cost you something.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-2xl mb-3">Financial calculators</h2>
        <p>
          The EMI, compound interest, FD, PPF, GST, sales tax, discount, commission and related
          calculators use standard published formulas. They are useful for estimating and for
          comparing options.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          They are <strong class="text-white">not</strong> quotes, and they will not match a
          lender's or tax authority's figure exactly. Real institutions apply processing fees,
          insurance, rounding conventions, day-count rules, compounding dates, prepayment
          penalties and rate revisions that a general calculator cannot know about. Statutory
          rates — GST slabs, tax brackets, PPF and FD rates — change, and a page may reflect a
          rate that has since moved.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Use these to get oriented. Confirm anything you will sign with your bank, lender, or a
          qualified financial adviser or chartered accountant. We are not registered financial
          advisers and nothing here is investment, tax or legal advice.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-2xl mb-3">Health and fitness tools</h2>
        <p>
          BMI, calorie, body-fat, water-intake, ideal-weight and similar tools apply population-level
          formulas. Those formulas are averages, and averages describe groups rather than people.
          BMI in particular does not distinguish muscle from fat and misreads athletes, older
          adults, pregnant people and children.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          <strong class="text-white">This is not medical advice, diagnosis or treatment.</strong>
          Nothing here substitutes for a doctor, dietitian or other qualified clinician. Do not
          start, stop or change any diet, exercise programme or medication because of a number on
          this site, and do not delay seeking medical advice because of one. If you may be having
          a medical emergency, contact your local emergency service now.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-2xl mb-3">Academic and student tools</h2>
        <p>
          CGPA, GPA, percentage and attendance calculators follow the conversion rules commonly
          used by Indian and international institutions. Grading schemes vary enormously between
          universities, and many apply their own weighting, rounding, credit rules and moderation.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Your institution's official result is the only one that counts. Verify against your
          university's own rules before relying on a figure for eligibility, applications or
          admissions.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-2xl mb-3">Document generators</h2>
        <p>
          Rent receipts, salary slips, experience letters, relieving letters and proforma invoices
          produce correctly formatted documents from the information you enter. They do not verify
          that information, and formatting is not legality.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          These templates are not legal advice and may not satisfy the requirements of your
          jurisdiction, employer or tax authority. You are responsible for the accuracy and
          legitimacy of what you enter and what you do with the result. Creating a document that
          misrepresents facts — to a landlord, an employer, a tax authority or anyone else — may
          be an offence. Have anything with legal or tax consequence reviewed by a qualified
          professional.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-2xl mb-3">File and conversion tools</h2>
        <p>
          PDF, image, text and data tools run in your browser. Conversion between formats is
          sometimes lossy by nature, unusual or corrupt files may not process correctly, and very
          large files can exhaust the memory your browser is allowed.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          <strong class="text-white">Always keep your original file.</strong> Because processing is
          local and nothing is uploaded, we hold no copy and cannot recover anything for you if a
          conversion goes wrong or a tab closes mid-operation.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-2xl mb-3">Accuracy and availability</h2>
        <p>
          We correct errors when we find them, but we do not warrant that every tool, formula, rate
          or article is accurate, complete or current. Tools may be changed or withdrawn, and the
          site may be unavailable at times.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          If you spot something wrong, please tell us — corrections from readers are genuinely
          useful and we act on them. The
          <a href="/contact/" class="text-violet-400 hover:text-violet-300 underline">contact page</a>
          is the fastest route.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-2xl mb-3">External links and advertising</h2>
        <p>
          Articles sometimes link to other sites for reference. We do not control them and are not
          responsible for their content or accuracy. Advertising is served by Google AdSense and
          selected by Google; an ad appearing on this site is not a recommendation from us.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-white font-semibold text-2xl mb-3">Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the fullest extent permitted by law, TextWonder accepts no liability for any loss or
          damage arising from reliance on any tool, result or article on this site. Your use of
          the Service is at your own risk, on the terms set out in our
          <a href="/terms/" class="text-violet-400 hover:text-violet-300 underline">Terms of Service</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="border-t border-slate-800 pt-6">
        <p class="text-sm">
          See also:
          <a href="/privacy-policy/" class="text-violet-400 hover:text-violet-300 underline">Privacy Policy</a> ·
          <a href="/cookie-policy/" class="text-violet-400 hover:text-violet-300 underline">Cookie Policy</a> ·
          <a href="/terms/" class="text-violet-400 hover:text-violet-300 underline">Terms of Service</a>
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
